{
  "$schema": "folio-block-summaries/v1",
  "entry": "10665-67132",
  "summaries": [
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-001",
      "source": "sections/page-001.md",
      "source_hash": "c07f03bcf4b50f7c190f9e17657d756872add8bfea94e152fe8e0322a5edfd56",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "The title page of the 2001 WHO research tool for assessing breastfeeding and replacement feeding practices in the context of mother-to-child transmission of HIV.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-002",
      "source": "sections/page-002.md",
      "source_hash": "7b4926c4c105b72fe62688b6e595dc9423df29973e2f3c73f553a3abd5ead05f",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "The copyright notice, stating that the document is not a formal WHO publication but may be freely reviewed, reproduced or translated for non-commercial use.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-003",
      "source": "sections/page-003.md",
      "source_hash": "5562fc262af5e2b9b7b1382286535417fd851002517a9614b834657ab7d83ca2",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "The table of contents of the infant feeding assessment tool, listing sections on risk factors, rationale, definitions, breast and infant mouth conditions, questionnaire modules, timing, data presentation, references and acknowledgements.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-004",
      "source": "sections/page-004.md",
      "source_hash": "46ba6a2bfce4be69417c19e701ab9f87fe627f00bcf38a71a4bf93662cb1425b",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Introduces the tool as guidance for researchers studying how infant feeding patterns relate to mother-to-child HIV transmission, building on existing indicators. A table gives estimated transmission rates during pregnancy, labour and breastfeeding with and without breastfeeding.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-005",
      "source": "sections/page-005.md",
      "source_hash": "1df4a5fc7a98cee7760628a6152904d676c92292b59ea90956de47f9d9cae576",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes risk factors for HIV transmission through breastfeeding, including high maternal viral load, low CD4/CD8 ratio and the duration of breastfeeding. It cites a study in which exclusively breastfed infants had lower transmission at six months than those also given other fluids or foods.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-006",
      "source": "sections/page-006.md",
      "source_hash": "375928ccb18fccf3f839d0e67becf30fbef122c37f2a1b25d41f3604d90a8749",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Completes the account of the study showing lower transmission among exclusively breastfed infants and notes its limitations. It then lists possible mechanisms by which exclusive breastfeeding might lower risk, such as protecting the infant's gut and immune system and maintaining breast tissue integrity.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-007",
      "source": "sections/page-007.md",
      "source_hash": "342072918039a5401e86d46fe48cc54d17220bfb0d595547fc4e3f4b07ebc796",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains that the tool was developed to gather more information on transmission risks through breastfeeding and to standardize definitions so that studies can be compared and risks quantified by feeding pattern.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-008",
      "source": "sections/page-008.md",
      "source_hash": "c607939de2b694fe9afa5182c08f5f6f377facb4dacc36c255365884a5a7921f",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Gives definitions of breastfeeding terms, drawing on indicators agreed at a 1991 WHO meeting, such as exclusive, predominant and mixed breastfeeding, and explains folk fluids. It explains that these common measures are used to assess practices and monitor breastfeeding promotion.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-009",
      "source": "sections/page-009.md",
      "source_hash": "0f9fa4a4f7ded7e4b5ded18af1e595829a1f6c13bc080944e07051a977f2f695",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Defines replacement feeding, describing suitable breast-milk substitutes in the first six months and enriched family foods afterwards.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-010",
      "source": "sections/page-010.md",
      "source_hash": "0780feaf56a731b377fe1b9d3b995cc7b948f8f5fe14c00d930741afb63c9600",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes breast conditions such as full and engorged breasts, mastitis and nipple problems, and infant mouth conditions such as thrush and ulcers, drawing on WHO breastfeeding counselling and mastitis documents.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-011",
      "source": "sections/page-011.md",
      "source_hash": "0e395411498a0af8e02db5740290e93ef4ae557bbdd4be70b99eb3a33959c068",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Introduces the six questionnaire modules on baseline data, feeding practices, maternal health, breast health, infant health and cessation of breastfeeding, and stresses training field workers before use.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-012",
      "source": "sections/page-012.md",
      "source_hash": "a863de45f34edc3410ec42f2a1bb32d627fb82aaca5d1abe89d21870da83b4da",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Module 1 lists baseline data to collect at recruitment, such as the mother's education, age, marital status, reproductive history, household and delivery details and birth weight, plus optional items.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-013",
      "source": "sections/page-013.md",
      "source_hash": "d8624f9ea3559c702e91162d58ff850c9987f8aa708a796d4832753f7b5a4e55",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Module 2 explains how feeding practices are assessed by asking whether specific items were ever given and how often during a recall period, rather than only over the previous 24 hours. It notes options such as repeated cross-sectional surveys or maternal diaries.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-014",
      "source": "sections/page-014.md",
      "source_hash": "fbd06786ff652a7cd9a7d51dc4a164c0e5a8adf8eabe063790c4766271278352",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains why the first week of life needs special attention, given complex feeding patterns, illness and separation of mother and infant, and introduces questions on items given in that week and why.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-015",
      "source": "sections/page-015.md",
      "source_hash": "b3426de016a85490213828f5aaf27ab7d7fe2f0c8e7209b710da4c0b514c078e",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "A table for recording foods and liquids given to the infant before the first breastfeed and during the first week, with reason codes.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-016",
      "source": "sections/page-016.md",
      "source_hash": "b0bd36059788ec64933ae5e65e85277de21cd4d4edae8cb58996758e85d77932",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Questions for follow-up visits on oral polio vaccine, foods and liquids given since the last visit and daily breastfeeds over the past week, with probing questions to check the answers.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-017",
      "source": "sections/page-017.md",
      "source_hash": "3a0b58b23fe0ab895460c12cbe1cc4c1bf6a12c2b906f453828d7846c8801820",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Additional questions on whether the mother has been separated from the infant and on night-time and comfort breastfeeding.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-018",
      "source": "sections/page-018.md",
      "source_hash": "0922c0baef3376c8f8562d2d8b141111c3f33743f2d07c773fa01f42cd41c489",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Notes defining the recall periods used in the feeding tables, such as yesterday and the six days before, and breast milk given during the day or night. It suggests some studies may also record feeding utensils, how they are cleaned, and pacifier use.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-019",
      "source": "sections/page-019.md",
      "source_hash": "3a59ef93f868a2bd5fd1327714927c692255ff6f48fe75fe22a9a55f8faa8874",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Questions on wet-nursing, asking whether anyone else breastfed the infant, how often, why and who.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-020",
      "source": "sections/page-020.md",
      "source_hash": "8fd47526d069635f93682a0144c7e04e7cd2bbbbe6f452b1d8f83819d8ba6ca0",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Questions on expressing breast milk, whether it was given to the infant or heat-treated and why, with notes on recording feeding utensils.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-021",
      "source": "sections/page-021.md",
      "source_hash": "9df97fc85689234baab9646ccc924b87f07753a561498e8c885838fc387c8ceb",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Module 3 explains that maternal health is recorded to rule out reverse causality, since a sick mother may change how she feeds her infant, and lists questions on maternal illness and resulting feeding changes.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-022",
      "source": "sections/page-022.md",
      "source_hash": "ee1e69971cea1cfbeaec9238052132fa1f22e9fa918aa2541ae58537bd7ed005",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Module 4 gives questions on breast health problems and their timing, symptoms and whether the infant fed from the affected breast, worded for field workers without health training.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-023",
      "source": "sections/page-023.md",
      "source_hash": "003999d0943113a9474f0edf7c06931ec4ffdfb13a052b926b4bebcaece4fb99",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Further questions on difficulties with breastfeeding and their causes, with advice to observe a breastfeeding session and to set up referral for mothers with breast problems.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-024",
      "source": "sections/page-024.md",
      "source_hash": "7fa0de6f4000673f5a2a918f8b364d50322f03da1f2250685a635eba9e1382cb",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Module 5 gives questions on infant weight and signs such as mouth sores and thrush, other illnesses and hospitalization, noting that some studies may use verbal autopsy for infant deaths.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-025",
      "source": "sections/page-025.md",
      "source_hash": "4416d5efa537714dc94aeaee91e2b4d02be2dfdc0036e3e935b273aafb1ab9cb",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Module 6 gives questions on when and how breastfeeding stopped, including methods used to stop.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-026",
      "source": "sections/page-026.md",
      "source_hash": "2476c85a50f767dfd565c12a93ccc296cfb8085c98177e2ae2effa9f863ff218",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Lists problems mothers may report when stopping breastfeeding, such as infant distress, breast pain or engorgement and disapproval by family or health workers.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-027",
      "source": "sections/page-027.md",
      "source_hash": "26fc39c0c956872256db6bde9aa3ddf31c8d16c67c5c1fb91c11f0b70d25f281",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Recommends applying the questionnaire first at 4–6 weeks after birth, ideally every two weeks for two months, then monthly to 6 months and every 3 months thereafter, and lists key time points for testing.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-028",
      "source": "sections/page-028.md",
      "source_hash": "bc21b6edc82a65096d41976f75120c73b0502f7dd17ed9089b97ab076037f4a7",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Recommends grouping infant feeding data into categories based on when different items were introduced and outlines the analysis of transmission risk by feeding pattern. The text still contains an editor's comment about renumbering a table.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67132/blocks/prose-page-029",
      "source": "sections/page-029.md",
      "source_hash": "a7ca950bc01ce8c5aa27a9e2db446c1760aa93d81572fd3a287236877b525326",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Lists infant feeding categories of special interest, such as exclusive breastfeeding with or without medicines, and suggests survival regression models with time-varying covariates.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
